[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Monster or Fish?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.44]What was the monster called? | 那个怪物叫什么？
[00:15.27]Fishermen and sailors sometimes claim to have seen monsters in the sea. | 渔夫和水手有时声称看到过海里的妖怪。
[00:21.92]Though people have often laughed at stories told by seamen, | 虽然人们常常嘲笑水手们讲的故事，
[00:27.10]it is now known that many of these 'monsters' which have at times been sighted are simply strange fish. | 但现在得知，人们有时看到的这些“妖怪”很多不过是些奇怪的鱼。
[00:36.82]Occasionally, unusual creatures are washed to the shore, but they are rarely caught out at sea. | 一些异常的生物偶尔会被冲到岸上来，但很少在远海被捕获。
[00:45.77]Some time ago, however, a peculiar fish was caught near Madagascar. | 然而不久前，在马达加斯加附近海域捕到了一条奇特的鱼。
[00:53.36]A small fishing boat was carried miles out to sea by the powerful fish as it pulled on the line. | 这条力气巨大的鱼拖着渔线，把一条小渔船拖到了数英里以外的海上。
[01:02.23]Realizing that this was no ordinary fish, the fisherman made every effort not to damage it in any way. | 渔民意识到这不是一条普通的鱼，于是千方百计不使它受到丝毫伤害。
[01:13.66]When it was eventually brought to shore, it was found to be over thirteen feet long. | 终于把它弄上岸后，发现它身长超过13英尺。
[01:21.91]It had a head like a horse big blue eyes, shining silver skin, and a bright red tail. | 它长着一个像马一样的头，大大的蓝眼睛，闪闪发光的银色皮肤和鲜红的尾巴。
[01:31.54]The fish, which has since been set to a museum where it is being examined by a scientist, is called an oarfish. | 这条鱼后来被送到博物馆，正由一位科学家进行研究，它被称为桨鱼。
[01:41.93]Such creatures have rarely been seen alive by man as they live at a depth of six hundred feet. | 人们很少看到活着的这类生物，因为它们生活在600英尺深的海下。
